  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency relief of Nutrition, Food Security, Shelter and Protection status among internally displaced population or IDP camps in Mon State.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltspan style=&quot;font-family:&quot;gtThis project will be
implemented by the integrated approach of emergency relief with Nutrition, Food
Security, Shelter, and Protection&#xa0;sectors. We will plan to make the
participatory rapid assessment (PRA) with the local CSOs and volunteers from
IDP camps. RM will plan integrated sectors which to provide maternal cash
transfer, nutritional assessment (MUAC or weight measurement)&#xa0;providing
nutrition package such as nutritious food supply package,&#xa0;multivitamin and
minerals for pregnant&#xa0;mothers and lactating mothers (Vitamin A and
Vitamin B1&#xa0;for Lactating&#xa0;Mother, Sprinkle
Micronutrients&#xa0;Powder,&#xa0;Vitamin A, Vitamin B1,&#xa0;Plumpynut for
under five children, weight measurement/MUAC assessment&#xa0;for under 5 years
children and pregnant women and lactating mothers,&#xa0;&#xa0;emergency food
rations and Shelter&#xa0;facilities for the needed IDPs&#xa0;in respective
townships in Mon State. Rain Maker will provide the technical and financial
support for systematic routine support and procurement for the emergency food
supports (such as fortified rice, blended oil, salts, onion, noodle, canned
etc.) and shelter facilities by combination with local resource and technical
and financial supports from RainMaker.&#xa0;Additionally, the project considers
on the sustainability of the food security of IDP through facilitate to adopt
temporary or short-term agriculture and livestock activities and protection
mainstreaming&#xa0;activities (capacity building and preparation for IDPs about
the Early Warning Response (EWR) system, airstrike preparation and Gender Based
Violence and Mining Awareness Activities) among&#xa0;IDPs and IDP camps. Protection
mainstreaming activities are capacity building and preparation for IDPs about
the Early Warning Response (EWR) system, airstrike preparation and Gender Based
Violence and Mining Awareness Activities.&#xa0;
The integrated approach on emergency response on IDPs will cover
Kyaikhto, Bilin, Thaton and Ye Townships in Mon state.lt/spangtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
